# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/octo-3 window (octo-T8 and its three levers on the fused stack; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/octo-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq arm needs its binary; every other arm runs that
# binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# L1 (TIMED, the ARM of the first ABAB pair): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3 = the control plus QWEN_FAST_OCTO=live (every eligible 8-live round
# is an octo round, no alternation), the octo draft, the bundled attention (4 users a launch) and the glue levers at eight-row users, and the third block's memory plan (the
# KV pool 19,968 to 16,500 blocks: four full 262,144-token windows still fit, 8 x 120,800 tokens reserve 15,112 of the 16,492 usable blocks). The same tests as C1. TIMED:
# the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. The two _long tests are this window's DEEP tests: eight
# real-code prompts of about 32k / 120k tokens with budgets (3,000 / 4,000, ignore_eos) that outlast the prefill queue, so that the last user arrives while the first is
# still decoding and eight seats decode together at depth; the 800-token concurrent8_code_32k / _128k (run beside them for continuity) never have six seats live at once, so
# no octo round runs in them and they read NO LOSS below six live seats. The octo-2 card runs' "bundle 4% slower at 32k" was exactly that: no octo round in the test at all,
# and a thread race that put the last arrival's decode alone at 51 or 31 tok/s. READ: c2_smoke_check clean AND python3 scripts/ci/octo_judge.py --container-log <container
# log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3 clean: one "[OCTO] admitted mode=live" line, the UNQUALIFIED lines, at least 16 rounds with
# shape=octo at 8 live and rows=8 (the positive control: written after the octo block's own verify counter moved), no counted m3 round under live, no program compiled on
# the first octo round, the K64j geometry line (extent replay engaged segments=8 flags=0x21 ... G8B1) and the factory line for the bundle's launch size (entries=4
# kv_share=false), and the lever rules: the octo draft engaged once and serving at least half of the 8-live octo rounds, the bundle engaged ONCE (the latch: the warm and
# the captured fixture build one bundle) with its call line, the glue8 engaged line for every site at users=8 rows=8 and 48 layers, no fallback, disabled or fell-back line
# anywhere. Then the pair: python3 scripts/ci/octo3_report.py --control-a <C1 smoke> --arm-a <L1 smoke> --control-b <C2 smoke> --arm-b <L2 smoke> --arm-container <L1
# container> --arm-container <L2 container> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3: per test (concurrent8_steady, concurrent8_code_32k_long,
# concurrent8_code_128k_long) the aggregate of the all-live window against the control's in BOTH pairs, the floors, GAIN / PARITY / LOSS; SHIP-GO needs no LOSS and a GAIN
# in the steady window; octo_compare.py for the texts (EVERY answer equal; any difference is NO-GO). The octo rounds' own numbers: python3 scripts/ci/octo2_report.py is NOT
# used (it pairs an octo boot against an octo boot); read the [OCTO] round lines' step_ms and gap_ms for the octo block's trace (86.5 ms on the Lever N stack) and the early
# draft's draft_ms. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; read
# telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A gain that comes with a different loaded AICLK between
# the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): 65 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k,concurrent8_code_32k_long,concurrent8_code_128k_long
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=100
